{"n": 1022, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "1022.webp", "text": "51-757\n\n5171414 INSTALLING REAR SPOILER (M-SYSTEM) Cars With Standard Rear Spoiler:\n\nRemove plastic nuts on inside of trunk lid and\nPainting: take off standard spoiler,\nThe panel of o rear spoiler is supplied with a prime coat and substructure paint coat,\nso that only the final paint coat has to be sprayed on.\nProcedures: BMW Plastic Part Painting.\nBMW Acrylic paint + 20 % BMW softface additive.\nImportant!\nMaximum enamel baking temperature: 50° C (122° F) — higher temperature could\nlead to deformation,\n\nTaping:\n— Soak a clean cloth in washing gasoline or cold cleaner and wipe off surfaces to be\n\ntaped.\n\n— Position and press on the double-sided adhesive tape (heated hand warm prigr to\napplication!).\n\n— Pull off protective backing and press on part at least 5 to 10 seconds. Initial\nadhotion can be improved by heating the body.\n\nPaint the panel’ (refer to “Painting”).\nInstall adhesive tape (1) (refer to “Taping™).\n\nDrill holes in trunk lic of cars not having a standard rear spoiler. Install approximately\n30 mm (1.181) wide adhesive tape across entire width of lid at distance K to lower\n\nedge of the trunk lid. Draw centerlines of holes from middle and lower edge of trunk\nlid (use measuring tape), punch and drill 7.5 mm (0.295\") dia, holes.\n\nK = 110 mm (4.331) a@ = 125 mm (4.9217) . *\nA = S65 mm (22.244\") b = 127 mm (5.000\") Fa at ES\nB = 346 mm (13.6272~) ¢ = 129 mm (5.079)\n\nC = 118 mm (4.646\")\nD = 130 mm (5.118)\nPull off adhesive tape carefully. Deburr and coat edges of holes with zinc dust paint.", "words": [["51-757", 0.4813, 0.0297, 0.551, 0.0535], ["5171414", 0.0838, 0.0681, 0.1303, 0.0806], ["INSTALLING", 0.1434, 0.0681, 0.2965, 0.0806], ["REAR", 0.2162, 0.0654, 0.2429, 0.0872], ["SPOILER", 0.2495, 0.0681, 0.2944, 0.0806], ["(M-SYSTEM)", 0.3005, 0.0681, 0.3687, 0.082], ["Cars", 0.7631, 0.0654, 0.7869, 0.0872], ["With", 0.7909, 0.0654, 0.8121, 0.0872], ["Standar